// Global type overrides for swag (tools/swag/swag.sh passes this file).
//
// Both types below are declared over a standard library type - `type FileMode
// os.FileMode`, `type Duration time.Duration` - so swag reads each as the integer
// enum of the constants it finds for the underlying type, collected from every
// package that declares them, in an order that changes between runs: the
// generated file differed on every `make gen-swag`. On the wire they are neither
// integers nor enums. MarshalJSON writes a string: an octal mode such as "0755",
// a duration such as "1h30m".
replace github.com/hivepaas/hivepaas/hivepaas_app/pkg/fileutil.FileMode string
replace github.com/hivepaas/hivepaas/hivepaas_app/pkg/timeutil.Duration string
